166:{"timestamp":"2026-07-31T14:54:59.818Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_02ffbd9b32d59991016a6cb74196748190816cc899f7613b8e","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The closed frame eliminated the bogus cell branch. The remaining residual is only K’s symbolic map normalizer failing to reduce “insert fresh key, then delete that same key” back to the original map. I’m adding that guarded collection identity as a derived simplification lemma; it runs after MPY’s real `#pop` and neither skips the pop nor changes any observable state."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fb8a5-d140-7993-83b3-47cad071cf27"}}}
