+# Auditor command record
+
+All mutable work ran in `/tmp/audit-work/3-below-zero-audit`. Each referenced
+terminal log was captured with `script -q -e -c '<command>' <log>`; its final
+line records `COMMAND_EXIT_CODE`.
+
+## Toolchain and integrity
+
+```bash
+kompile --version && kprove --version && krun --version && python3 --version
+```
+
+Exit 0. K tools reported v7.1.293; Python reported 3.10.12. Log:
+`00-toolchain-versions.log`.
+
+```bash
+python3 /audit-output/evidence/stage1_integrity.py
+```
+
+Exit 0. All required records and candidate deliverables were regular, every
+declared file hash matched, all 1,093 JSONL events parsed, the campaign block
+matched the lock, the trace pipeline hash matched `usage.json`, and the two
+semantics trees were recursively identical. Log: `01-stage1-integrity-final.log`.
+
+## Translation and Python differential
+
+```bash
+python3 py2mpy.py solution.py | cmp - solution.mpy
+```
+
+Exit 0, no output: regenerated bytes equal submitted bytes. Log:
+`02-regenerate-mpy-byte-identity.log`.
+
+```bash
+python3 /audit-output/evidence/differential.py
+```
+
+Exit 0: `cases_checked=142270`, `mismatches=0`. Log:
+`02-python-differential.log`.
+
+## Clean concrete reconstruction
+
+```bash
+python3 py2mpy.py auditor-smoke.py > auditor-smoke.mpy
+kompile --backend llvm reference-semantics/semantics.k --main-module MPY-KRUN --syntax-module MPY-SYNTAX --output-definition runtime-audit-kompiled
+krun auditor-smoke.mpy --definition runtime-audit-kompiled
+```
+
+Each exited 0. The final configuration had `.K`, `NoExc`, empty stack, and exit
+code 0. Logs: `03-translate-smoke.log`, `03-kompile-llvm.log`, and
+`03-krun-smoke.log`.
+
+## Clean bridge-free proof reconstruction
+
+```bash
+kompile --backend haskell verification-base.k --main-module VERIFICATION-BASE --syntax-module MPY-SYNTAX --output-definition verification-base-audit-kompiled
+kprove connection-spec.k --definition verification-base-audit-kompiled --spec-module CONNECTION-SPEC --claims CONNECTION-SPEC.call-prefix-connection
+kprove connection-spec.k --definition verification-base-audit-kompiled --spec-module CONNECTION-SPEC --claims CONNECTION-SPEC.for-to-loop-connection
+kprove connection-spec.k --definition verification-base-audit-kompiled --spec-module CONNECTION-SPEC --claims CONNECTION-SPEC.loop-connection
+```
+
+Each exited 0; each individual claim printed `#Top`. Logs:
+`03-kompile-verification-base.log`, `03-kprove-call-prefix.log`,
+`03-kprove-for-to-loop.log`, and `03-kprove-loop.log`.
+
+## Clean target reconstruction and adequacy probes
+
+```bash
+kompile --backend haskell verification.k --main-module VERIFICATION --syntax-module MPY-SYNTAX --output-definition verification-audit-kompiled
+kprove spec.k --definition verification-audit-kompiled --spec-module SPEC --claims SPEC.below-zero
+kprove context-spec.k --definition verification-audit-kompiled --spec-module CONTEXT-SPEC --claims CONTEXT-SPEC.continuation-containment
+python3 /audit-output/evidence/pinning_check.py
+```
+
+Each exited 0. Both K claims printed `#Top`; the pinning check reported exact
+constructor identity after normalizing only the two parser spellings of empty
+`Stmts`. Logs: `03-kompile-verification.log`, `03-kprove-target.log`,
+`04-kprove-context.log`, and `04-pinning-check.log`.
+
+```bash
+kprove auditor-ground-summary-spec.k --definition verification-base-audit-kompiled --spec-module AUDITOR-GROUND-SUMMARY-SPEC
+```
+
+Exit 0 and `#Top` for the corrected configuration-shaped ground claims. Log:
+`04-kprove-ground-summary-corrected.log`. An earlier functional-claim spelling
+was rejected by the backend as unsupported before execution (exit 113,
+`04-kprove-ground-summary.log`); that diagnostic was not used as proof evidence.
+
+```bash
+kprove auditor-body-sensitivity.k --definition verification-audit-kompiled --spec-module AUDITOR-BODY-SENSITIVITY --claims AUDITOR-BODY-SENSITIVITY.subtract-body
+```
+
+Expected exit 1 with `WarnStuckClaimState`; fixed execution reached `true` while
+the mutated claim required `false`. Log: `04-kprove-body-sensitivity.log`.
+
+## Exhaustive static inventory
+
+```bash
+python3 /audit-output/evidence/rule_inventory.py
+```
+
+Exit 0. It inventoried 1,125 declarations/rules/claims from all 28 selected K
+sources into `rule-inventory.tsv`; see `05-rule-inventory-final2.log`.
+
+## Fresh false-postcondition mutation
+
+```bash
+kprove auditor-false-postcondition.k --definition verification-audit-kompiled --spec-module AUDITOR-FALSE-POSTCONDITION --claims AUDITOR-FALSE-POSTCONDITION.positive-list-is-true --dry-run
+kprove auditor-false-postcondition.k --definition verification-audit-kompiled --spec-module AUDITOR-FALSE-POSTCONDITION --claims AUDITOR-FALSE-POSTCONDITION.positive-list-is-true
+```
+
+The dry run exited 0. The proof then exited 1 with `WarnStuckClaimState` at a
+reachable final `<k> false </k>` while the mutation required `true`. Logs:
+`06-false-postcondition-dry-run.log` and `06-false-postcondition-proof.log`.
